## 1. Objective
In `TDB-738`, Tenuto added single-note click-and-drag pitch transposition on the Piano Roll. However, when working with multi-track arrangements or layered chords, users need to repitch **all music on a given beat** simultaneously by holding **`Shift`**.

This contract implements **Beat-Wide Pitch Transposition (`Shift + Click` & `Shift + Drag`)**:
1. **Shift + Click Any Pitch Row or Piano Key (`piano-roll-row-<midi>` / `piano-key-<midi>`):** Holding `Shift` and clicking any pitch row on the Piano Roll grid (at a beat column) or clicking a target row after Shift-selecting a beat computes the semitone delta from that beat's anchor note to the clicked pitch row and transposes **every note and chord on that beat** across the score in a single atomic `.ten` source mutation.
2. **Shift + Click & Drag Any Note on a Beat:** Holding `Shift` while dragging any note vertically locks all notes on that beat together—moving every note and chord on that beat in unison in the live optimistic preview and updating all of their tokens in `.ten` code on mouse release.
3. **Reverse-Offset Multi-Span AST Patcher (`transposeBeatEventsInSource`):** Deduplicates chord spans, skips unpitched drum grid hits (`style=grid`), and patches `.ten` source spans from back to front (`sourceStartOffset` descending) so multi-track beat mutations never shift character offsets.

---

## 2. Root Cause
1. `src/mutator/TopologicalMutator.ts` only mutates one event span at a time (`replaceEventInSource`) and lacks a reverse-sorted multi-span beat mutator (`transposeBeatEventsInSource`) to transpose all tracks/voices on a beat simultaneously without offset drift.
2. `src/components/WebGPUCanvas.tsx` does not check `e.shiftKey` on note mouse-down or pitch-row clicks to group all events sharing `startWhole`.
3. `src/components/SplitWorkspace.tsx` (`handleCanvasMutation`) only processes a single `eventData` token rather than routing beat-wide mutations (`eventData.isBeatWideMutation`) through `transposeBeatEventsInSource`.

